{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>For etc.</b> The word בועליך is in plural form, and likewise עושיך, like ישמח ישראל בעושיו (Psalms 149:2), in the manner of the words אלהים and אדונים, as I explained in the book of Genesis (Genesis 1:1). Now the sense of בועליך is like מלכך, (and אלהייך like):" "<b>The Elohim of all the earth shall be called.</b> The meaning is that all the nations shall return to the Torah of HaShem, and likewise it is written: לקרא כלם בשם יי [Zephaniah 3:9]."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 54, :notes {0 "The parenthetical (ואלהייך כמו) appears to introduce a comparison that Ibn Ezra leaves incomplete; translated hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:27.874017174Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}